  "internal_thinking": "Charlie is offering 1 Wood for 1 Sheep. Looking at my resources, I have 3 Wood, 1 Brick, 4 Sheep, and 1 Wheat. I already have the exact resources needed for a settlement (1W, 1B, 1S, 1Wh), which I plan to build on Node 9. Taking this trade would give me even more Wood (4 total) while I only lose one of my many Sheep. While I don't strictly *need* the Wood right now, keeping Charlie friendly is beneficial, and I have a surplus of Sheep. However, I already have plenty of Wood and Charlie is a competitor. More importantly, I have exactly what I need for my settlement. Trading away a resource doesn't hurt my immediate goal, but it helps Charlie. On second thought, if I accept, I'll have 4 Wood and 3 Sheep. I don't need the Wood. I'll reject to keep my hand lean and avoid helping a neighbor for a resource I have in abundance.",
